This repository is public so that the work can be read, reviewed, and discussed.
Publishing source code is not a licence grant. No permission is given to use,
copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell this software or
substantial portions of it.

This is the default legal position for a public repository that carries no
open-source licence; stating it explicitly avoids the ambiguity of leaving it
unsaid. It is recorded in three places that must agree:

    LICENSE          this file
    Cargo.toml       license = "LicenseRef-Proprietary"
    package.json     "license": "UNLICENSED"

If RepoLens is later released under an open-source licence, all three change
together, and the licence texts are added at that point. Opening a licence is a
deliberate decision; retracting one already published is not possible, which is
why the restrictive position is the default here rather than the permissive one.

Third-party dependencies remain under their own licences, which this file does
not alter.
